      "Title": "Exam GED Section 5 Mathematics topic 1 question 1 discussion - ExamTopics",
      "Question": {
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "value": "Danny worked 40 hours and earned $6.30 per hour. His friend Erica earned $8.40 per hour at her job. How many hours would Erica have to work in order to equal"
          },
          {
            "type": "break"
          },
          {
            "type": "text",
            "value": "Dannys earnings for 40 hours?"
          }
        ]
      },
      "Choices": {
        "A": {
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "value": "A. 20"
            }
          ]
        },
        "B": {
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "value": "B. 25"
            }
          ]
        },
        "C": {
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "value": "C. 30"
            }
          ]
        },
        "D": {
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "value": "D. 252"
            }
          ]
        },
        "E": {
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "value": "E. Not enough information is given."
            }
          ]
        }
      },
      "Answer": {
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "value": "Suggested Answer: C \ud83d\uddf3\ufe0f"
          },
          {
            "type": "break"
          },
          {
            "type": "text",
            "value": "Danny earned a total of 40($6.30) = $252. To find the number of hours Erica would take to earn $252, divide $252 by $8.40."
          }
        ]
      },
      "Explanation": {
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "value": "Danny earned a total of 40($6.30) = $252. To find the number of hours Erica would take to earn $252, divide $252 by $8.40."
          }
        ]
      },
